# ==============================================================================
# PYTHON - SHARED DEFAULTS (the python pack)
# ==============================================================================
# The template the scaffolding targets use when they are called directly, by
# name. `fnew` never reads it: it always picks from the catalog interactively.
#
# `gmake env_global_enable` copies this block into
# ~/.config/zsh/gmake/.env.global the first time it runs; after that it only
# adds what is missing.
#
# Nothing reads this file: it is a sample. The filled copy in .env.global is
# what gmake loads.
#
# Both lines stay commented out on purpose: a sample's comments do not travel
# into the .env, so leaving them out means "unset, and the target will ask".
# Uncomment one to pin a default for every project on this machine.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Optional default template for direct copier_project/cruft_project calls ---
# PROJECT_TEMPLATE_REPO=
# PROJECT_TEMPLATE_VERSION=
